{
    "background_story": "Fiona was a talented baker who inherited her love for traditional German breads from her Oma. Among her specialties was zwieback, a classic twice-baked bread that was a staple in her family for generations. Fiona's zwieback was renowned for its crispy crust and soft interior, making it a favorite among the locals. She would often tell the story of how her Oma used to bake zwieback for the family during the holidays, filling the house with the warm, comforting aroma. As Fiona's bakery grew in popularity, she remained committed to using only the finest ingredients and time-honored techniques to create her signature zwieback. Her dedication to preserving traditional baking methods earned her the title of 'Zwieback Queen' among the community, and her bakery became a beloved gathering place for those seeking a taste of nostalgia and warmth.",
